/inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MURATA HARUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ARAKI, SHINGO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IWASAKI, KENJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAWASE, ICHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MURATA, HARUO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A pigment composition in which an ester compound ordinarily used as a solvent and in other applications, such as butyl acetate or oleyl acetate, is used as a flowability improver for a pigment dispersion and which comprises a pigment and the ester compound as essential ingredients; and a pigment dispersion obtained by dispersing the pigment composition in a solvent, etc. The dispersion is significantly improved in pigment dispersibility and flowability. When the pigment composition or pigment dispersion is used in producing a color filter, a homogeneous film having high contrast can be obtained.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention se rapporte à une composition pigmentaire dans laquelle un composé ester habituellement utilisé comme solvant dans d'autres applications, tel que l'acétate de butyle ou l'acétate d'oléyle, est utilisé en tant qu'agent améliorant la fluidité d'une dispersion pigmentaire. Ladite composition comporte en tant qu'ingrédients essentiels un pigment et ledit composé ester. L'invention se rapporte également à une dispersion pigmentaire que l'on fabrique en dispersant la composition pigmentaire dans un solvant, etc. Cette dispersion se caractérise par une amélioration importante de la dispersibilité du pigment et de sa fluidité. Une telle composition pigmentaire ou une telle dispersion pigmentaire peut servir à la fabrication d'un filtre coloré présentant un film homogène à contraste élevé.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>